course: dictionary
lesson: 5066
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. To find the right one, read the words around it. «The Japanese artist Yayoi Kusama makes Infinity Mirror Rooms where mirrors and lights make the space look endless; art that fills a room is called an installation.» The room, the mirrors and the lights are clues, so an installation here is a large artwork that fills a space.
explain: The same word can mean something very different in another sentence. «The installation of the new boiler took all morning.» Now the clues are boiler and took all morning. An installation here means putting something in place so it is ready to use. Same word, different job.
explain: To check your answer, swap your meaning into the sentence. Does «a large artwork that fills a space took all morning» make sense? No, so you know it is not the art meaning here. Always check the clues first.
fact: Installation is a noun, and it comes from the verb to install.
fact: «Installation» can mean putting a machine, system or program in place so it is ready to use.
fact: In art, «installation» means a large work built in a room or space that people walk around or into.
fact: «Installation» can also mean a military or industrial base or building.
fact: A good check is to swap in your meaning and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «The installation of the new boiler took all morning.» What does installation mean here? | *Putting the new boiler in place so it is ready to use | A boiler that has broken down | A quick walk around the house | A large painting hung on a wall
exercise: «The artist's installation filled the whole gallery, and visitors walked through it.» What is an art installation? | *A large artwork that people walk around or into | A map of a city | A small drawing in a book | A type of cooking pot
exercise: Ava says, «The installation wizard helped me set up the app.» What did the installation wizard help with? | Drawing pictures in the app | *Putting the app on the computer so it is ready to use | Cleaning the computer screen | Ordering a new computer online
test: «The military installation sat on the edge of the town, behind high fences.» What does installation mean here? | *A military base, a place with buildings for an army | A museum of art | A kind of house for birds | A new computer program
test: Which sentence uses installation to mean a large artwork in a room? | *The gallery's installation of glowing lights filled the whole room | The installation of the bathroom tiles was messy | The military installation was closed for repairs | The software installation took ten minutes
exam: In «Yayoi Kusama makes Infinity Mirror Rooms where mirrors and lights make the space look endless», what makes the room look endless? | Paint on the floor | A long corridor | *Mirrors and lights | Loud music
